{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/929274-feral-vehicles","id":929274,"title":"Feral Vehicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-10T10:34:46-07:00","id":929274,"title":"Feral Vehicles","content":"The idea of feral vehicles is something I've been playing around with for a while, and I think they could fit in a lot of places and in a lot of the gamelines. Ruleswise, I'm torn between handling them as vehicles and working out something to handle the lack of drivers or using the horror rules. I also think it'd make sense to give them Numina, maybe even some unique ones. <br /> <br /> Mostly inspired by Genius the Trangression and the eventual fate of the flying car from Harry Potter. <br /> <br /> Rumors:<br /> <br /> - They're what happens when a species of animal is driven out of an area. A few spirits of that animal are leftover, and they end up trying to latch onto anything they can find. Out of those, a handful of them try to Claim or Ride inanimate objects, and vehicles are usually the main thing they go for. Toasters and staplers aren't as mobile. <br /> <br /> - They've got ghost drivers. There's some Numina that lets a ghost merge almost perfectly with one of its Anchors. It's not just standard Poltergeist activity, unfortunately. Once a ghost is merged with something, both of them get stronger. See, normally when a ghost tries to drive a car, it's a clumsy telekinetic fiasco. But when it's all merged in, it's got perfect control, incredible ability, all of that. And it...does something to their minds or whatever a ghost brain is called. You know that quote about hammers and nails? A ghost that's fused with a car is going to decide that most of its problems can be best handled by running them over. <br /> <br /> - It was some government project to create a psychic AI that wasn't bound to any one body and could pilot numerous different ones by basically possessing them. Probably escaped somehow. Unless the government just decided to dump it on us to see how it'd perform in the &quot;wild&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:43:21-07:00","id":929297,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I can't really comprehend anything you've typed because of the immediate image in my mind. This is what we are talking about now.<br /> <img src=\"http://pre15.deviantart.net/08fe/th/pre/i/2012/292/f/6/dragster_of_doom_by_spitfirelex-d5ht326.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-10-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:47:41-07:00","id":929300,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's fetish art but just something about it makes my subconscious vaguely uncomfortable in the way fetish art does. <br /> <br /> If it helps, I was actually thinking about Werecar Bender when I wrote the original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:03:24-07:00","id":929313,"title":"","content":"What about Christine and The Car? Those count under the ghost/spirit classification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:05:00-07:00","id":929315,"title":"","content":"I mean, going back to talking about this seriously, yeah, those would be inspirations, as would Maximum Overdrive. <br /> <br /> Does DtD have anything regarding entirely mechanical cryptids? Like, a machine that gets whanged up by infrastructure and basically becomes a robot? <br /> <br /> I could totally see a car or other vehicle left in the Hedge coming to life, assuming the hobs don't strip it for parts first. That's probably what the ChroD version of the Flying Ford Anglia would be, some Mage's enchanted car that crashed in the Hedge and came to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:31:45-07:00","id":929445,"title":"","content":"Beetlejuice references aside, this sounds like it'd be an interesting thing to throw into a campaign. I might try this with the playtest I'm running of Dragon, where one of the characters is a mechanic who keeps working on cars. Actually, I think you could write a whole thing up on how to use it: does anyone want to try and build mechanics on this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/929274-feral-vehicles?p=929315#post929315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could totally see a car or other vehicle left in the Hedge coming to life, assuming the hobs don't strip it for parts first.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I had the opposite happen once, where a tar-like Changeling was the infinite-gasoline-supply of an engine some high level characters had bought off of some Fey who'd been experimenting with stuff. (This was a post-revelation campaign, continuing another campaign which involved a few war.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:47:30-07:00","id":929464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/929274-feral-vehicles?p=929315#post929315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, going back to talking about this seriously, yeah, those would be inspirations, as would Maximum Overdrive.<br /> <br /> Does DtD have anything regarding entirely mechanical cryptids? Like, a machine that gets whanged up by infrastructure and basically becomes a robot?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, not as such, but one of the cryptid mutations can change the composition of the cryptid, if a cryptid can be made out of nuclear waste, cement, or fire, then an animal or plant becoming mechanical hardly seems implausible. <br /> <br /> Some hobgoblins are biomechanical in nature, so a hobgoblin car doesn't seem far fetched.<br /> <br /> Also in road trip, it discusses the possibility of ghost or even revenant cars, so how about cars that aren't possessed by ghosts but are ghosts? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:50:16-07:00","id":929465,"title":"","content":"Here, this might actually be a good place for the community to show an example of how to make a new Template. This would go really well with some of the stuff in Midnight Roads, especially if there was a 4 or 5 dot merit to actually be able to drive one of these cars. Someone, make a doc off of something like this...<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Monster Car Template</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">X-Splat: - What made the car supernatural in the first place</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Animal</b> - Biological components built in (Doomie)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Haunted</b> - Someone died in the car and is now operating from within.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Possessed</b> - External spiritual entity within the car. Can happen from someone caring about a car.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Computer</b> - Advanced technology (like Kit from Night Rider)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Fairy Dust</b> - The Fae did this shit, as usual. It might be a Changeling.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Stranger Things have Happened</b> - It could just be another unexplained phenomenon</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Y-Splat: <b>Driver</b> - What drives the car to do whatever it does?</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Beast</b> - It's like an animal, and does things according to bestial instincts.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Avenger</b> - Taking revenge for real or imagined slights</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Loyalty</b> - Loyal to a particular person, such as the mechanic who took it out of the junk yard and fixed it</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Hunger</b> - The car hungers for something, such as killing or adrenaline.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"> - </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Driverless</b> - No reason to keep doing things, so it probably goes dormant.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Attributes</b> - Does it need the full 9? Could it use &quot;Power, Finesse, Resistance&quot;?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Skills replaced by <b>Build</b> - The baseline physical traits of the car.</span><br /> 11 points at starting level.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Acceleration</b> - How much speed can change in one turn</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Aesthetics</b> - How good it looks</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Body</b> - How tough it is</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Handling</b> - How well it can make turns</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Reliability</b> - How likely something is to break</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Size</b> - Is it a big car or a little car? (0 is a smart-car, 5 is a truck)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Speed</b> - The top speed the engine can drive</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Traction</b> - How well it sticks to the road during tight maneuvers</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>No Merits</b>: how would it have Barfly or know Karate?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Physical Powers: <b>Mods</b> - Physical modification to the car itself</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Armor Plating</b> - Natural Armor: 1/1 per dot</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Spoilers</b> - Negate penalties to Handling and Traction at high speeds</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Hopper Suspension</b> - Car can propel itself into the air to &quot;Jump&quot;</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Nitrous Injector</b> - Provides a sudden boost to speed and acceleration</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Paint Job</b> - Extra-Nice Paint adds special bonuses to Aesthetics and, if not damaged, Willpower</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Weaponry: Melee</b> - Spikes, Spears, anything that can be used for ramming and shearing attacks.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Weaponry: Guns</b> - There is a gun of some sort attached to the car of quality relating to the number of dots. To make the gun hidden in some way, add a dot to the cost.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernatural Powers: <b>Decals</b> - Crazy powers the car has through supernatural means, used by spending Fuel.</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Body Work</b> - Car repairs itself</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Chicken</b> - Force drivers of other cars into </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Deer in the Headlights</b> - pedestrians are prevented from moving out of the way without rolling to resist this first</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Jump the Hump</b> - Car can get serious airtime</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Spider Wheels</b> - Drive on surfaces which are too steep to drive on without falling off, like walls</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Transformer</b> - Can take on a different shape with a different Build</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Health replaced by <b>Structure</b>, because it's a machine.</span><br /> Determined by Size + Body<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">They also have <b>Willpower</b>, because they are conscious entities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pool: <b>Fuel</b> - Whatever's keeping that car going, it's not just Gasoline...</span><br /> Used For...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Turning the Engine on</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Running for an amount of time</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Activating Decals</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Sudden Bursts of Speed</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Regained by...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Getting Gasoline or whatever is supposed to fuel it (Diesel or electricity)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Killing people for a reason specified by Driver</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Being worked on (for cars driven by Loyalty)</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Supernatural Trait: <b>Pistons</b> - How intensely supernatural is this thing?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Integrity Trait: <b>Sentience</b> - How coherent is it? Higher levels are actualy able to articulate and communicate, like Kit. Mid levels might just be kind of bestial. At the bottom levels it only acts occasionally. At 0, it turns back into a normal car, retaining Mods but not Decals.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:11:28-07:00","id":929472,"title":"","content":"Werewolves have an ability that allows them to basically Claim a vehicle. If their body dies while they do so, the werewolf is then fully part of the vehicle and develops strange new abilities, likely variants of its existing ones.<br /> <br /> There's also ways to awaken the spirits of objects like vehicles. You don't necessarily need an animal spirit as spirits as a whole are predatory creatures. I believe one of the examples in Predators is a truck spirit that developed into an accidents and pain spirit that enjoys running over people and crushing their bones.<br /> <br /> Anyways since these things are physical and not ephemeral, you might just use Dread Powers rather than Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:11:18-07:00","id":929492,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=856916#post856916\"><b>Reighnhell wrote one of these using the Brief Nightmares system (Midnight Titan).</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:35:55-07:00","id":929507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/929274-feral-vehicles?p=929492#post929492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=856916#post856916&amp;quot;]</a><b>Reighnhell wrote one of these using the Brief Nightmares system (Midnight Titan).</b>[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of my inspirations, yeah. But that template looks super sweet. I might want to simplify it even more, though, and make it into something you could slap on to any existing vehicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:41:23-07:00","id":929509,"title":"","content":"If you'd like some more inspirational material, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_Wizards\" target=\"_blank\">Young Wizard</a> series has a whole alternate earth populated with killer cars.<br /> <br /> As a <i>distantly </i>related aside, the car in <a href=\"http://stephenking.wikia.com/wiki/Buick_Roadmaster\" target=\"_blank\">From a Buick 8</a> always struck me as pretty Intruder-ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}